From eb6e5491c1e42d8b67f166cca3f1ff6cef295fa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] perf(render): remove per-draw allocations in optimized
 renderer

Every optimized draw applied two VertexAttributeStates, each cloning
VertexAttributeType.values(), and model matrices allocated a 64-byte heap
buffer plus a float view. Every queued draw also hashed its MaterialProperties
and VertexAttributeState through Objects.hash varargs arrays.

Redirect the values() call to a shared array that is only iterated, and the
matrix buffer to a per-thread buffer with the same capacity and byte order;
Utilities.store writes all 16 absolute indices before the same absolute reads.
Both hashCode methods compute the Objects.hash value over the same fields in
the same order without the array. GL calls, their order and arguments are
unchanged. The compatibility test checks these call sites and field orders in
the bundled Mappings classes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
